        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "885f08ed-5ed7-50e1-a756-c8de49a7be40",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, George Weinberg, Dutch Schultz, Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Salvatore Maranzano\n- Roles: mobster, mob hitman, gunman, mob accountant, associate\n- Places: New York City, Manhattan\n- Events: Manhattan Bootleg Wars, gangland slayings\n\nFacts:\n- George Weinberg was born in 1901 and later became a New York mobster.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll was born as Uinseann Ó Colla on July 20, 1908, and he became an Irish American mob hitman in New York City during the 1920s and early 1930s.\n- During the 1920s and 1930s, George Weinberg and his brother Abraham Weinberg were associates of Dutch Schultz, and George Weinberg served as a mob accountant.\n- During the Manhattan Bootleg Wars, Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg became one of Dutch Schultz's top gunmen.\n- Abraham \"Abe\" Weinberg was later a suspect in the gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and Salvatore Maranzano.\n- Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll died on February 7, 1932.\n- George Weinberg died on January 29, 1939.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
