        "text": "Page: Abraham Weinberg. Sentence: Abe Weinberg would become one of Schultz's top gunmen during the Manhattan Bootleg Wars and was a later suspect in the high-profile gangland slayings of Jack \"Legs\" Diamond, Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll, and mob boss Salvatore Maranzano.\nPage: Mad Dog Coll. Sentence: Vincent \"Mad Dog\" Coll (born Uinseann Ó Colla, July 20, 1908 – February 7, 1932) was an Irish American mob hitman in the 1920s and early 1930s in New York City.\nPage: George Weinberg (mobster). Sentence: George Weinberg (1901 – January 29, 1939) was a New York mobster and, with brother Abraham Weinberg, an associate of Dutch Schultz as a mob accountant during the 1920s and 1930s.",
